ining each anchor to its predecessor."", "The field is named prev_root rather than a digest of the complete prior signed anchor document.", "Two successive runs over an unchanged store necessarily have the same Merkle root while potentially differing in generated_at, signature, signer, and other document metadata. A later prev_root equal to that shared root cannot distinguish which document was its predecessor.", "Repository retrieval could not be attempted in this harness, so the implementation may differ from the artifact's description." ], "falsifier": "Show that prev_root is actually a collision-resistant digest of the complete canonical, signed predecessor document, or that another signed field uniquely commits to that predecessor's document digest.", "confidence": "likely", "novel_vs_prior": "novel" }, { "id": "F3", "claim": "The command called publish has no enforceable publication postcondition because it only prints git commands, so successful local anchor creation can be mistaken for an externally witnessed publication.", "severity": "major", "location": "scripts/provenance_anchor.py publish behavior", "evidence": [ "The artifact states: "The CLI prints those commands and executes none."", "It also describes the public-git publication as the mechanism that moves the fact outside operator control.", "Without executing or subsequently checking the push, the CLI cannot establish that the tag exists remotely, that the expected commit is reachable from it, or that any third party observed it." ], "falsifier": "Show a mandatory, machine-checked publication receipt or a post-push verification step that confirms the exact root-bearing ref and commit on an independent remote before reporting publication success.", "confidence": "verified", "novel_vs_prior": "novel" }, { "id": "F4", "claim": "A public git push does not by itself create a durable third-party witness, and placing the root in a tag name or commit message changes event visibility but not the absence of 