ation, or replacement can observe different files at different instants. Signing that aggregate makes it authoritative even if no single filesystem instant had that leaf set.", "Repository retrieval and execution were unavailable, so the absence of locking or a retry-until-stable implementation could not be confirmed." ], "falsifier": "Show code and tests establishing a coherent snapshot, such as a shared writer lock, filesystem snapshot, immutable generation directory, or a stable double-scan that also detects in-place changes and directory-entry races.", "confidence": "speculative", "novel_vs_prior": "novel" }, { "id": "F6", "claim": "The ADR-18 adopt-before-build gate is not satisfied by the recorded process because the anchor-specific alternatives review was neither independent nor completed before the custom construction was built.", "severity": "major", "location": "Governance status and prior-art reasoning", "evidence": [ "The artifact states: "The tier-2 reuse review has not been performed. This review is that review."", "It also states that the cited survey "is about a different subsystem" and that "the anchor's own survey" was conducted by a single model family.", "The artifact says ADR-18 requires "adopt before extend before compose before build" and tier-2 review across at least three provider surfaces and four model families.", "The custom mechanism was therefore already built and published before the required anchor-specific reuse gate was completed.", "Repository and external-system retrieval were unavailable, so no comparative implementation assessment of Rekor, SCITT, Trillian, OpenTimestamps, or certificate-transparency tooling was possible." ], "falsifier": "Produce a pre-build, anchor-specific ADR-18 record satisfying the required provider and model-family coverage and documenting why adopted mechanisms fail concrete requirements that outweigh the custom code's security and maintenance cost.", "confidence": "verified", "novel_vs_prior": "novel" }